nt is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 12.2% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 22%.","Capex runs 1.9x depreciation (6.8% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 34, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 5.8% a year to shareholders (5.0% in buybacks and 0.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 17.5% of the float, 3.6 days to cover."],"people":["With about 345 employees, each generates about $2.0M of revenue, 5.3x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 24.5% a year.","That works out to $306K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.7M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $72K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":55,"head":"Avoid: priced 109% above its fair value of $78.06.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 55, gates 14/25)","ROIC 55.2% vs WACC 9.1%","FCF margin 15.2%","Revenue grew 22.9%/yr over 5y","Returns 5.8% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 109% above fair value of $78.06","Net debt/EBITDA 5.0x","P/E 38.2x vs sector 19.3x","EV/EBITDA 23.9x vs sector 11.2x","P/FCF 41.8x vs sector 16.5x"],"flags":["Priced 109% above its fair value of $78.06"],"need":[],"buy_below":66.35,"vc":{"base":78.06,"base_src":"dcf","bear":45.84,"bull":126.46,"alt_median":31.39,"n_alt":2,"gap":1.4871,"dispersion":0.2602,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 149% above the other models' median ($31.39)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_